Slide 1: Proposed Research Topic
- Utility of Blockchain for Cross-Border Payment and Real World Asset Tokenisation
- PhD Research Proposal

---
Slide 2: Introduction
- Blockchain: Distributed ledger technology enabling secure, transparent transactions
- Cross-border payments: Challenges (cost, speed, transparency)
- Real world asset tokenisation: Converting physical assets (real estate, commodities, etc.) into digital tokens
- Growing interest in financial innovation and digital transformation

---
Slide 3: Objectives of the Research
- Analyze blockchain’s impact on cross-border payment efficiency
- Evaluate benefits and risks of asset tokenisation
- Identify regulatory, technical, and adoption challenges
- Propose frameworks for secure, scalable implementation

---
Slide 4: Proposed Research Methodology
- Literature review: Academic papers, industry reports
- Case studies: Existing blockchain payment and tokenisation platforms
- Data analysis: Transaction speed, cost, security metrics
- Interviews: Industry experts, regulators
- Comparative analysis: Traditional vs blockchain-based systems

